 "note": "Where a token like 'lunch' can lead. 'cafe', 'grocer', 'garden', 'market', 'stop', 'clinic' mean the resident's nearest one. 'bank', 'library', 'museum', 'cinema', 'dealer' likewise (Tools/worldgen/add_places_01.py). 'playground', 'noticeboard', 'kiosk' likewise, and 'play' is the children's list (Tools/worldgen/add_dressing_01.py). 'furniture' likewise: the furniture outlet (Tools/worldgen/add_outlet_01.py). lunch near_work: on a working day lunch is taken near work (the nearest café, grocer or market to the workplace), and at home only when home is within near_work_home_max_m of work (CITY-096, owner 2026-11-23) [ASSUMPTION]. 'mall' (CITY-106; the owner, 2026-11-24: 'update population to come to mall'): the place 'mall' in a list is the mall with outlets nearest the resident's home, where they 'shop' at a place before a counter or 'eat' at a table. It is gone to only when the resident's own start of that part of the day is between 'open' and 'last_in' (so they are served before the keepers go home); and only when that part of their day is long enough to walk there, stay 'stay_min' minutes and walk home; otherwise they do what 'else' says for that list. 'shops_shut_sunday': on a Sunday its shop owners are at home like the town's shopkeepers, so nobody goes there to shop, only to eat at its food outlets, which are kept. 'staff_eat_in': those who work at such a mall eat their lunch at its tables and do not leave it. The shares (3 of the 24 ways to spend free time, 1 of 9 shopping trips, 1 of 13 on a rainy day) and the hours are first guesses [ASSUMPTION].",
